    "media:imagetext": "AP\nFor Your Safety\n737-800\nIf you are sitting in an overwing window exit row please identify yourself to a crew\nmember to allow for reseating if: You lack the ability to read, speak, or understand\nthe language, or the graphic form, or the ability to understand oral crew commands\nin the language specified by the airline.\nPara su Seguridad\nSi está sentado en una ventana de salida sobre las alas, sírvase identificarse con\nun miembro de la tripulación para que lo cambie de asiento si: No puede leer,\nhablar o entender el idioma, o forma gráfica, o no entiende las órdenes verbales de\nla tripulación en el idioma especificado por la aerolínea\nPour votre Sécurité\nSi vous êtes assis près d'une rangée à proximité du hublot issue de secours aile,\nveuillez le signaler à l'un des membres de l'équipage pour qu'il puisse vous trouver\nun autre siège si : vous ne pouvez pas lire, parler ou comprendre la langue ou le\ngraphique ou si vous ne pouvez pas comprendre les instructions orales de\nl'équipage dans la langue spécifiée par la ligne aérienne.\nFür Ihre Sicherheit\nWenn Sie in einer Ausgangsreihe über dem Flügel sitzen, melden Sie sich bitte bei\neinem Crew Mitglied, damit Ihnen einen neuer Sitz zugewiesen werden kann, wenn:\nSie die Sprache bzw. die graphische Form nicht lesen, sprechen oder verstehen\nkönnen oder die mündlichen Anweisungen der Crew in der von der Fluggesellschaft\nvorgeschriebenen Sprache nicht verstehen können.\nPara sua Segurança\nO seu assento é numa janela sobre a asa de fila de saída; por favor identifique-se a\num membro da tripulação para possibilitar um novo assento se: não falar, ler ou\ncompreender a língua, ou o gráfico, ou não entender as instruções verbais da\ntripulação na língua especificada pela companhia aérea.\nEmergency exits are often heavy, awkward to lift, push, pull, and maneuver when opening.\nBecause of this, and for the safety of all passengers, Federal Law requires that we only seat\nqualified passengers next to exits. If you are sitting in an exit row, you may be asked to open\nthe exit and assist our crew in the event of an emergency. Please ask to be reseated if you:\n• Have a physical condition which may not be visible which may prevent you from helping.\n• Lack the strength, mobility, dexterity, or balance required to open the exit and assist our crew\n• Do not think you could reach the exit, open it, and get out quickly.\n• Believe the physical exertion required to open the exit would injure you.\n• Are hearing impaired and could not hear commands from our crew.\n• Lack sufficient visual capacity to perform one or more of the applicable duties without the\nassistance of visual aids beyond contact lenses or eyeglasses.\n• Are not able to give oral commands to others.\n• Do not understand the instructions in this brochure.\n• Have other responsibilities (such as a small child to care for) which would prevent you from\nhelping.\n• Are less than 15 years old\n• Do not wish to help in this way.\nFederal regulations require all passengers, regardless of where they\nare sitting or\ntheir physical condition, to review this card, for their safety.\nFederal regulations require customer compliance with lighted information signs,\nposted placards, areas designated as non-smoking, and crew member instructions\nwith regard to these items.\nWhen finished reviewing this card, please return it to the seat pocket for our next customer.\nPM0395 (Rev. 6/01)",
